    "text": "The equation of state for a gas is given by <math> <mrow> <mtext>PV</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>nRT</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mi>&#945;</mi> <mtext>V</mtext> </mrow> </math>,&nbsp;where n is the number of moles and <math> <mrow> <mi>&#945;</mi></mrow> </math>&nbsp; is a positive constant. The initial temperature and pressure of one mole of the gas contained in a cylinder are T<sub>0</sub> and P<sub>0</sub> respectively. The work done by the gas when its temperature doubles isobarically will be :",
